      "kind": "question",
      "question": "Should the cache key include the locale?\nThe parsed form differs only in the error messages, which are translated.",
      "status": "escalated",
      "created_at": "2026-11-24T09:48:02.000Z",
      "context": {
        "background": "The cache stores each parsed file under a key made from its path and its content hash. Error messages are translated at parse time, so a cached file parsed under one locale would show its errors in that locale under another.",
        "if_yes": "The key gains the locale. A machine that switches locale parses once more per locale; nothing else changes.",
        "if_no": "Messages are translated when shown instead of at parse time: a larger change, about two more days of work in the parser.",
        "recommend": "yes",
        "why": "It is the smaller change and keeps the parser as it is; the extra parse per locale is rare."
      }
    },
